From: liuqin Fedora maintainers <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: liuqin: disable the unused QCE consumer

Source: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/f18bbcc84540750d948b17776687fe2e491b81a1
7.3.1 already has QCE runtime PM code, but the driver is gated by BROKEN.
The deployed kernel therefore has an enabled, unbound consumer rather than
an active QCE instance with the old fixed 393600 bandwidth request.
Disable the unused node so it cannot hold its interconnect suppliers'
sync_state pending. Keep cryptobam, SCM, UFS ICE and all crypto config gates.
An isolated RAM comparison must verify both Build ID and this DT status;
the kernel Image does not change when only the DT is changed.
No battery-life claim follows from a bandwidth-vote observation alone.
Validation and rollback: tasks/upstream-refresh/RESULT.md.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -2239,3 +2239,8 @@
 &cs35l41_tr { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
 &cs35l41_br { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
 &cs35l41_bl { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
+
+/* No driver is available with the upstream BROKEN gate retained. */
+&crypto {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
